melody:
# Chorus as published in 1928 (cut time, written here with quarter-note beats; the dotted
# eighth + sixteenth figures are as printed)
An-oth-er bride, an-oth-er June,
D4// E4/. D4// B4(2) ~B4/. D4// E4/. D4// C5(2) ~C5/.
an-oth-er sun-ny hon-ey-moon,
D4// E4/. D4// D5(2) ~D5/. G4// A4/. G4// D5(2) ~D5/.
an-oth-er sea-son, an-oth-er rea-son
C5// D5/. C5// B4 B4 ~B4/. D4// E4/. D4// Bb4 Bb4 ~Bb4/.
for mak-in' whoop-ee!
G#4// A4/. A#4// B4 G4(3) ~G4 r r/.
A lot of shoes, a lot of rice,
D4// E4/. D4// B4(2) ~B4/. D4// E4/. D4// C5(2) ~C5/.
the groom is nerv-ous, he an-swers twice.
D4// E4/. D4// D5 D5 ~D5/. G4// A4/. G4// D5(2) ~D5/.
It's real-ly kill-ing that he's so will-ing
C5// D5/. C5// B4 B4 ~B4/. D4// E4/. D4// Bb4 Bb4 ~Bb4/
to make whoop-ee!
G#4/ A4/ ~A#4/ B4 G4(3) r(4)
Pic-ture a lit-tle love-nest,
D5/ F5 D5/ F5 D5 C5 C5(3)
down where the ros-es cling,
C5/ Eb5 C5/ Eb5 C5 B4(2) r(2)
pic-ture the same sweet love-nest,
D5/ F5 D5/ F5 D5 C5 C5(3)
think what a year can bring.
C5/ Eb5 C5/ Eb5 C5 B4(2) ~B4/.
He's wash-ing dish-es and ba-by clothes,
D4// E4/. D4// B4 B4 ~B4/. D4// E4/. D4// C5(2) ~C5/.
he's so am-bit-ious, he ev-en sews,
D4// E4/. D4// D5 D5 ~D5/. G4// A4/. G4// D5(2) ~D5/.
but don't for-get, folks, that's what you get, folks,
C5// D5/. C5// B4 B4 ~B4/. D4// E4/. D4// Bb4 Bb4 ~Bb4/.
for mak-in' whoop-ee!
G#4// A4/. A#4// B4 G4(3) r(2) r/.

# Once more (the second chorus words)
An-oth-er year or may-be less,
D4// E4/. D4// B4(2) ~B4/. D4// E4/. D4// C5(2) ~C5/.
what's this I hear? Well, can't you guess?
D4// E4/. D4// D5(2) ~D5/. G4// A4/. G4// D5(2) ~D5/.
She feels ne-glect-ed, and he's sus-pect-ed
C5// D5/. C5// B4 B4 ~B4/. D4// E4/. D4// Bb4 Bb4 ~Bb4/.
of mak-in' whoop-ee!
G#4// A4/. A#4// B4 G4(3) ~G4 r r/.
She sits a-lone 'most ev-'ry night,
D4// E4/. D4// B4(2) ~B4/. D4// E4/. D4// C5(2) ~C5/.
he does-n't 'phone her, he does-n't write.
D4// E4/. D4// D5 D5 ~D5/. G4// A4/. G4// D5(2) ~D5/.
He says he's "bu-sy," but she says "is he?"
C5// D5/. C5// B4 B4 ~B4/. D4// E4/. D4// Bb4 Bb4 ~Bb4/
He's mak-in' whoop-ee!
G#4/ A4/ A#4/ B4 G4(3) r(4)
He does-n't make much mon-ey,
D5/ F5 D5/ F5 D5 C5 C5(3)
on-ly five thou-sand per;
C5/ Eb5 C5/ Eb5 C5 B4(2) r(2)
some judge who thinks he's fun-ny
D5/ F5 D5/ F5 D5 C5 C5(3)
says "You'll pay six to her."
C5/ Eb5 C5/ Eb5 C5 B4(2) ~B4/.
He says, "Now judge, sup-pose I fail?"
D4// E4/. D4// B4 ~B4 ~B4/. D4// E4/. D4// C5(2) ~C5/.
The judge says, "Budge right in-to jail.
D4// E4/. D4// D5 ~D5 ~D5/. G4// A4/. G4// D5(2) ~D5/.
You'd bet-ter keep her, I think it's cheap-er
C5// D5/. C5// B4 B4 ~B4/. D4// E4/. D4// Bb4 Bb4 ~Bb4/.
than mak-in' whoop-ee!"
G#4// A4/. A#4// B4 G4(3) ~G4(2) ~G4 r
